WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.906 --> 00:00:19.229
Mary led Dickon down the path to the place where the ivy grew thickly on the garden wall.

2
00:00:20.469 --> 00:00:24.752
Dickon felt as if he were being taken to look at a rare bird's nest and must move

3
00:00:24.812 --> 00:00:30.675
softly. When Mary stepped to the wall and lifted the hanging ivy, Dickon jumped back.

4
00:00:31.695 --> 00:00:32.536
There was a door!

5
00:00:34.204 --> 00:00:37.427
Mary slowly opened it, and they walked into the garden.

6
00:00:37.447 --> 00:00:40.009
"Here is the secret garden.

7
00:00:41.069 --> 00:00:43.611
I'm the only one in the world who wants it to be alive."

8
00:00:43.631 --> 00:00:47.694
"This is a strange, pretty place," he whispered.

9
00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.936
"It's like we're in a dream."

10
00:00:52.738 --> 00:00:56.601
For two or three minutes, Dickon simply stood there looking at the garden.

11
00:00:57.762 --> 00:00:59.984
Then he began to walk around softly.

12
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.043
He walked even more lightly than Mary had walked the first time she had entered the garden.

13
00:01:05.063 --> 00:01:09.948
"I never thought I'd see this place," he said at last in a whisper.

14
00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:12.029
"Did you know about it?"

15
00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:14.031
asked Mary in her normal voice.

16
00:01:15.712 --> 00:01:16.813
Dickon made a sign to her.

17
00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:22.398
"We must talk quietly, or someone will hear us and wonder what's going on in here."

18
00:01:22.418 --> 00:01:24.860
"Oh, I forgot!"

19
00:01:25.401 --> 00:01:29.224
said Mary, feeling frightened and putting her hand quickly to her mouth.

20
00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.681
"Did you know about the garden?"

21
00:01:32.101 --> 00:01:33.402
she asked again quietly.

22
00:01:34.682 --> 00:01:35.343
Dickon nodded.

23
00:01:35.363 --> 00:01:36.543
"Martha told me.

24
00:01:37.684 --> 00:01:39.245
We used to imagine what it was like."

25
00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:45.308
He stopped and gazed in wonder at the tangle of climbing roses in the trees.

26
00:01:45.328 --> 00:01:49.170
"Oh, the bird nests that will be here in springtime!

27
00:01:50.271 --> 00:01:52.832
It'll be the safest nesting place in England."

28
00:01:54.333 --> 00:01:55.974
Mary put her hand on his arm.

29
00:01:55.994 --> 00:01:58.215
"Will there be roses?"

30
00:01:58.776 --> 00:01:59.356
she whispered.

31
00:02:00.384 --> 00:02:02.025
"I thought perhaps they were all dead."

32
00:02:03.766 --> 00:02:05.246
"No. Not all of them.

33
00:02:05.686 --> 00:02:06.187
Look here."

34
00:02:06.847 --> 00:02:08.668
Dickon stepped over to a rose bush.

35
00:02:10.469 --> 00:02:13.950
He pulled a knife from his pocket and cut a lifeless-looking stem.

36
00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.391
"There's still green in that wood.

37
00:02:16.811 --> 00:02:17.332
Look at it."

38
00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.653
Mary was down on her knees in a moment.

39
00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:24.995
"When it looks a bit greenish and juicy like that, it's alive."

40
00:02:25.495 --> 00:02:26.556
He cut another stem.

41
00:02:27.724 --> 00:02:31.908
"But when the inside is dry and breaks easily like this, it's done for.

42
00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:34.150
There's a big root here.

43
00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.913
If it's cared for, there'll be a fountain of roses this summer."

44
00:02:39.494 --> 00:02:40.795
Mary smiled brightly.

45
00:02:41.235 --> 00:02:42.557
The roses were alive!

46
00:02:43.718 --> 00:02:47.961
The robin followed them as they went from bush to bush and from tree to tree.

47
00:02:49.122 --> 00:02:53.366
Dickon knew how to cut away the dry wood and could tell when a stem still had life

48
00:02:53.426 --> 00:02:53.646
in it.

49
00:02:54.887 --> 00:02:57.581
Within half an hour, Mary thought she could tell too.

50
00:02:59.123 --> 00:03:01.544
Mary's new gardening tools proved quite handy.

51
00:03:02.685 --> 00:03:07.169
Dickon showed her how to use the fork, while he dug about roots to let the air in.

52
00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.933
They were busy working around a big rose bush, when he caught sight of something.

53
00:03:11.953 --> 00:03:14.235
"Who did that?"

54
00:03:14.735 --> 00:03:18.318
He pointed to one of Mary's own clearings around the pale green points.

55
00:03:18.338 --> 00:03:20.199
"I did."

56
00:03:20.219 --> 00:03:24.042
"Why, I thought you didn't know anything about gardening."

57
00:03:24.062 --> 00:03:25.684
"I don't.

58
00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:29.455
But they were so little, and they looked as if they had no room to breathe.

59
00:03:30.656 --> 00:03:31.897
So I made space for them.

60
00:03:32.338 --> 00:03:33.639
I don't even know what they are."

61
00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:39.744
"You did exactly the right thing," said Dickon, kneeling next to the tiny plants.

62
00:03:41.045 --> 00:03:42.827
"A gardener couldn't have told you better.

63
00:03:43.808 --> 00:03:46.630
They're crocuses and snowdrops and daffodils."

64
00:03:47.971 --> 00:03:51.955
They agreed that there was a lot of work to be done and that Dickon would come to

65
00:03:52.015 --> 00:03:53.076
help her every day.

66
00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.903
"I wouldn't want to make the garden look too neat," he said cautiously.

67
00:03:57.923 --> 00:04:03.166
"No, it wouldn't seem like a secret garden if it was too tidy."

68
00:04:03.186 --> 00:04:09.391
"This is a secret garden, sure enough, but I think someone else besides the robin has been working

69
00:04:09.431 --> 00:04:09.791
in here.

70
00:04:11.032 --> 00:04:13.834
Some pruning has been done more recently than ten years ago."

71
00:04:13.854 --> 00:04:16.595
"But how could anyone get in?"

72
00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.096
Mary was puzzled.

73
00:04:19.638 --> 00:04:21.119
Dickon shrugged his shoulders.

74
00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:22.860
"Let's plant your seeds."

75
00:04:24.124 --> 00:04:26.746
Mary held the seeds, while Dickon loosened the earth.

76
00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:31.809
"You're just as nice as Martha said you were," she said, smiling at him.

77
00:04:31.829 --> 00:04:39.214
"Now I like five people: you, Martha, your mother, Ben, and the robin."

78
00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:41.756
"Only five people!"

79
00:04:43.377 --> 00:04:47.660
Dickon laughed so hard he had to put his hand over his mouth to stifle the sound.

80
00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.822
"Do you like me?"

81
00:04:50.302 --> 00:04:51.483
Mary asked quietly.

82
00:04:51.503 --> 00:04:53.044
"I do.

83
00:04:53.556 --> 00:04:54.597
And so does the robin."

84
00:04:55.097 --> 00:04:58.299
He nodded toward the bird, who was perched on a tree nearby.

85
00:04:58.319 --> 00:05:00.600
"That's two for me then."

86
00:05:01.061 --> 00:05:01.961
She looked pleased.

87
00:05:03.122 --> 00:05:06.584
Just then the big clock in the courtyard struck Mary's lunch hour.

88
00:05:06.604 --> 00:05:10.346
"I have to go," she said sadly.

89
00:05:11.907 --> 00:05:14.228
She started toward the door but turned around.

90
00:05:14.248 --> 00:05:19.872
"Whatever happens, you would never tell anyone about the secret garden, would you?"

91
00:05:21.128 --> 00:05:25.877
"If you were a bird and showed me where your nest was, I'd never tell," Dickon promised.

92
00:05:25.897 --> 00:05:28.642
"Your secret is safe with me."

93
00:05:30.124 --> 00:05:31.847
And Mary was quite sure it was.
